how to increase dom performance

    for(let i=0;i<img.length;i++)
    {
        con.innerHTML+=`<img alt="Employee in the company" class="team-img" src="${img[i]}">`
    }
    this manipulates dom multiple times 
    
    instead we can add it to an empty string and then we can just add at the end to increase performance and not always modifying dom is right 
    let imgsDOM=""
    for(let i=0;i<img.length;i++)
    {
        imgsDOM+=`<img alt="Employee in the company" class="team-img" src="${img[i]}">`
    }
    con.innerHTML=imgsDOM